# Commits

Commit each finished slice. One purpose per commit. Do not batch unrelated work.

Subject line only. No body, no period, and no pull request number.

```
[chore]: cursor rules
[chore]: gitignore
[feat]: fee curve
[fix]: fee clamp
[test]: inventory vectors
[update]: strategy params
[docs]: architecture notes
[ci]: forge workflow
[upgrade]: hook redeploy
```

Classes: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `test`, `docs`, `update`, `upgrade`, `ci`.

Join two or three nouns with ` + ` when one commit covers them. Stay on one line.

No em dashes, en dashes, or hyphens in the subject. No extra brackets or parentheses. The class brackets are the whole prefix.

One feature per branch. Use a short branch name. The pull request title copies the feature commit subject.
